# chronyd's options; chrony.service reads DAEMON_OPTS (docs/build.md, "Time").
# -F 1: the distribution's system call filter.
# -s: at start, set the clock from the real-time clock, or, on a board
#     without one (Raspberry Pi 4), to the time chronyd last stopped (the drift
#     file's time), so the clock never starts before the last run while NTP
#     is out of reach. systemd-timesyncd did this with its clock file.
DAEMON_OPTS="-F 1 -s"

# Ubuntu's chrony.service: not in a container.
SYNC_IN_CONTAINER="no"
